Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Bobby Comet <griffin.linux@gmail.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pyqt6, pkexec | policykit-1, gnupg, curl
Recommends: dkms, software-properties-common
Conflicts: xkm, xkm-multi-kernel-manager
Replaces: xkm, xkm-multi-kernel-manager
Provides: xkm, xkm-multi-kernel-manager
Homepage: https://github.com/bobbycomet/XKM-Multi-Kernel-Manager
Description: Griffin Kernel Manager for Linux (APT, pacman, dnf, zypper)
 GKM is a PyQt6 GUI for installing, removing, holding/unholding and
 tracking Linux kernels. It detects the distribution (and the base distro
 of derivatives) and the hardware, and manages the kernels that fit:
 mainline, XanMod and Liquorix on Debian/Ubuntu systems (other families
 are supported by the AppImage build).
 .
 It handles repository setup, package holds, a bootloader refresh safety
 net after install/remove, and DKMS rebuilds for newly installed kernels,
 with a reboot prompt once everything is ready.
 .
 All privileged operations are performed by a small dedicated helper
 script authorised via a scoped polkit policy, rather than granting the
 whole application root privileges.
